Chapter: TextureKernel
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 Texture mapping from Codex [Device] AST: a Mode-7-style perspective ground
 plane. One GPU thread per pixel projects the pixel onto an infinite textured
 floor, tiles the world coordinate into a 256x256 texture the host uploaded into
 a storage buffer, samples the texel (device-load), and fogs it by distance. The
 floor scrolls with the frame. This is the reference site's "texture" technique
 -- the sampling and perspective are real Codex, reading a real uploaded texture.

 The texture is a 256x256 array of packed RGB integers at binding 0; the output
 framebuffer is binding 1. Integer fixed point throughout.

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  tx-width : Integer = 1024
  tx-half-w : Integer = 512
  tx-horizon : Integer = 300
  tx-focal : Integer = 420
  tx-scale : Integer = 52000

Section: Tiling and Colour

  tx-tile : Integer -> Integer
  tx-tile (w) = let m = w - (w / 256) * 256 in if m < 0 then m + 256 else m

  tx-sky : Integer -> Integer
  tx-sky (py) =
    let h = py * 255 / tx-horizon
    in let r = 20 + h * 20 / 255
    in let g = 30 + h * 40 / 255
    in let b = 60 + h * 120 / 255
    in r * 65536 + g * 256 + b

 Fog by screen-space depth: far (near the horizon, small sy) fades to a haze.

  tx-shade : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tx-shade (texel) (fog) =
    let r = texel / 65536
    in let g = texel / 256 - (texel / 65536) * 256
    in let b = texel - (texel / 256) * 256
    in let hr = 60
    in let hg = 70
    in let hb = 95
    in let sr = (r * fog + hr * (256 - fog)) / 256
    in let sg = (g * fog + hg * (256 - fog)) / 256
    in let sb = (b * fog + hb * (256 - fog)) / 256
    in sr * 65536 + sg * 256 + sb

Section: Texture Kernel

 Per pixel: below the horizon, perspective-divide to a ground distance, find the
 world coordinate (scrolling with the frame), tile it into the texture, sample,
 and fog. Above the horizon, draw the sky. The texel is always loaded (index 0
 for sky pixels) so the device-load is unconditional.

  texture-step : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  texture-step (texbuf) (outb) (frame) (gid) =
    let px = gid - (gid / tx-width) * tx-width
    in let py = gid / tx-width
    in let sy = py - tx-horizon
    in let sky = sy <= 0
    in let d = if sky then 1 else tx-scale / sy
    in let wx = (px - tx-half-w) * d / tx-focal
    in let wz = d + frame * 3
    in let u = tx-tile wx
    in let v = tx-tile wz
    in let idx = if sky then 0 else v * 256 + u
    in let fog = if sy > 256 then 256 else sy
    in act
    texel <- device-load texbuf idx
    let out = if sky then tx-sky py else tx-shade texel fog
    in device-store outb gid out
    end
